id: pm-pcy92t
title: Core command flag_invocations misclassify valueless booleans as required string values
description: "Command-scoped machine contracts derive several core boolean flags as takes_value:true and value_required:true (for example init --defaults, test --run, --progress, and --fail-on-skipped), contradicting Commander help and executable behavior. Unify core invocation arity with the canonical flag declaration so agents can safely synthesize invocations without scraping human help."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-18T06:30:42.678Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-18T23:07:52.141Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-18T21:13:48.364Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-18T21:13:48.364Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Every core boolean flag reports takes_value=false and value_required=false in command-scoped flag_invocations while value-bearing flags retain truthful required/optional/repeatable metadata.; A parity gate compares executable Commander arity with SDK flag_invocations for every core command and fails on a synthetic boolean/string mismatch.; Compact discovery remains within token budgets and generated contract fixtures, SDK docs, Node/Bun packed acceptance, and exact coverage are updated."
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make machine contracts sufficient and trustworthy for autonomous invocation synthesis
value: Agents avoid invalid retries and wasted context caused by boolean flags advertised as required strings
impact: "Corrects the universal SDK contract used by CLI, MCP, packages, and recursive self-improvement tooling"
why_now: Packed acceptance for positional/MCP parity reproduced the contradiction on multiple high-use core flags
parent: pm-usfg
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: fixed
expected_result: Core machine flag_invocations match executable Commander arity for every boolean and value-bearing option.
actual_result: "Independent parity verifies 2,904 declared and observed flags across 68 core commands with zero findings; mismatch negative control fails and packed Node/Bun acceptance passes."
